    <bpmn:process id="W_W1110" name="W1110. Vendor-Managed Inventory (VMI) Seasonal Ramp-Up &amp; Wind-Down" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal calendar event trigger (W306), S&amp;OP seasonal planning cycle (W133), or vendor-initiated seasonal forecast discussion
Frequency: Quarterly (aligned with Philippine seasonal patterns); ad-hoc for weather-driven events
Volume: 12 VMI vendors × 300 SKUs × 4 seasonal transitions = ~14,400 SKU-level parameter adjustments per year
Owner: Merchandise Planner (Supply Chain)
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Category Manager, VMI Vendor Account Manager, DC Operations Manager
Source: workflow W1110 — Vendor-Managed Inventory (VMI) Seasonal Ramp-Up &amp; Wind-Down</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1110_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1110_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1110_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1110_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1110_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1110_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1110_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1110_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1110_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1110_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1110_Start4" name="Seasonal calendar event trigger (W306), S&amp;OP seasonal planning cycle (W133), or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1110_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1110_Task5" name="Seasonal Demand Forecast Preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Seasonal Demand Forecast Preparation: (a) Merchandise Planner prepares seasonal demand forecast per VMI vendor and SKU: (i) pull 3-year historical sales data by month for each VMI SKU; (ii) apply seasonal index factors from Demantra (W31 — fit-gap C5): e.g., waterproofing items have a 3.0× seasonal index in Jun–Aug vs. annual average; aircon has a 2.5× index in Mar–May; (iii) adjust for known events: upcoming typhoon forecast (PAGASA), government infrastructure project pipeline, new store openings; (iv) calculate target inventory levels for the upcoming season: target weeks of supply = base weeks × seasonal multiplier; (b) Planner prepares seasonal parameter change proposal: current parameters → proposed parameters for each SKU (min/max/ROP/EOQ), expected impact on inventory value and service level
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1110_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1110_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1110_Task6" name="VMI Vendor Collaborative Planning Session">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: VMI Vendor Collaborative Planning Session: (a) Merchandise Planner and Category Manager meet with each VMI vendor&#x27;s account team (video call or in-person at HQ Davao): (i) present seasonal demand forecast and proposed parameter changes; (ii) vendor shares their production capacity constraints, lead time changes, and any supply-side risks; (iii) jointly agree on: seasonal safety stock levels, peak demand replenishment frequency (e.g., from weekly to twice-weekly deliveries), allocation priorities if supply is constrained; (iv) document agreed changes in VMI seasonal addendum to the vendor agreement; (b) for seasonal ramp-up: vendor commits to building buffer stock in their warehouse 4–6 weeks before season starts; (c) for seasonal wind-down: vendor agrees to reduce replenishment quantities 4 weeks before season ends to prevent excess inventory carry-over
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours per vendor × 12 vendors = 12–24 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1110_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1110_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1110_Task7" name="VMI System Parameter Update &amp; Vendor Transmission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VMI System Parameter Update &amp; Vendor Transmission: (a) Merchandise Planner updates VMI parameters in BuildRight&#x27;s ERP: new min, max, ROP, EOQ, safety stock, and target weeks of supply for each SKU; (b) system transmits updated parameters to vendor&#x27;s VMI portal (W866) via EDI/API; (c) vendor acknowledges receipt and confirms their system is updated; (d) system validates: if vendor&#x27;s system does not reflect updated parameters within 48 hours, automatic escalation to Category Manager; (e) parameters effective date set to the agreed seasonal transition date (e.g., &quot;Parameters effective June 1 for rainy season&quot;)
Responsible (R): System / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1110_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1110_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1110_Task8" name="Seasonal Transition Monitoring &amp; Exception Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Seasonal Transition Monitoring &amp; Exception Management: (a) during the 2-week transition period (1 week before to 1 week after effective date), system monitors VMI performance closely: (i) daily VMI fill rate (target ≥ 95%); (ii) inventory level vs. new target range (flag if &gt; 120% of max or &lt; 80% of min); (iii) replenishment order frequency vs. agreed rate; (b) exceptions handled: (i) if vendor over-ships during ramp-up (exceeding max): Merchandise Planner contacts vendor to hold shipments; excess inventory flagged for inter-store transfer (W22) or markdown (W93); (ii) if vendor under-ships during peak: emergency procurement (W60) triggered from alternative vendors; VMI service level credit applied per W245; (iii) if seasonal demand significantly deviates from forecast (&gt; ±20%): Planner adjusts parameters mid-season in consultation with vendor
Responsible (R): System / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min/day during transition period</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1110_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1110_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1110_Task9" name="Post-Season Review &amp; Wind-Down Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-Season Review &amp; Wind-Down Assessment: (a) at end of each season, Merchandise Planner prepares post-season review: (i) actual demand vs. forecast by SKU; (ii) inventory carry-over at season end (target: &lt; 2 weeks of supply); (iii) stockout incidents during peak; (iv) VMI vendor performance scorecard impact; (b) results fed into next season&#x27;s forecast calibration (W31) and VMI quarterly business review (W672); (c) remaining seasonal inventory disposition plan: markdown (W93), transfer to other stores still in season (W22), or return to vendor per buy-back agreement (W901)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 3–4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1110_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1110_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1110_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1110_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1110_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-249 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Portal &amp; Collaboration (PA-03.4).) | - operational: Merchandise Planner (Supply Chain) review and approval gate
Owner: Merchandise Planner (Supply Chain)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
