    <bpmn:process id="W_W1495" name="W1495. Vendor-Managed Inventory (VMI) Replenishment, Min/Max Review &amp; Automated PO Generation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Store inventory for a VMI-eligible SKU falls below the agreed minimum level; also monthly min/max parameter review cycle
Frequency: Continuous automated monitoring; monthly parameter review; quarterly VMI program performance evaluation
Volume: ~300 VMI SKUs across the assortment (per profile §6.4); ~12 key VMI vendor partners (per W1944/W5495); ~2,000–4,000 VMI-generated POs per month chain-wide
Owner: Merchandise Planner
Participants: Vendor Account Manager, Merchandise Planner, Receiving Associate, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1495 — Vendor-Managed Inventory (VMI) Replenishment, Min/Max Review &amp; Automated PO Generation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1495_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1495_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1495_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1495_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1495_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1495_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1495_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1495_Lane3" name="Receiving Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1495_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1495_Lane4" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1495_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1495_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1495_Start6" name="Store inventory for a VMI-eligible SKU falls below the agreed minimum level; also monthly…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1495_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1495_Task7" name="VMI min/max parameter setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: VMI min/max parameter setup: For each VMI-eligible SKU at each store: (a) Merchandise Planner sets minimum (reorder point) and maximum (target stock level) quantities; (b) parameters based on: (i) average daily sales velocity (last 90 days); (ii) supplier lead time (typically 3–7 days for domestic, 30–60 days for import); (c) safety stock buffer added for seasonal volatility; (d) parameters reviewed monthly and adjusted based on demand trends; (e) vendor accesses min/max parameters in portal and plans production/delivery accordingly
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month for parameter management</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1495_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1495_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1495_Task8" name="Automated PO generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automated PO generation: When store inventory for a VMI SKU drops below minimum: (a) system automatically generates a draft PO for the vendor: quantity = max − current on-hand − in-transit; (b) PO routed to vendor through the portal with expected delivery date; (c) vendor confirms fulfillment capability and proposed ship date; (d) if vendor cannot fulfill: alternative proposed (partial shipment, substitute SKU, delayed full shipment); (e) Merchandise Planner receives notification of any vendor-proposed changes and approves/rejects within 24 hours; (f) confirmed PO becomes a committed order in the system
Responsible (R): System / Vendor Account Manager
Accountable (A): Merchandise Planner
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1495_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1495_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1495_Task9" name="VMI delivery &amp; receipt">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VMI delivery &amp; receipt: (a) vendor ships against confirmed PO; (b) delivery arrives at store or DC per the routing guide; (c) Receiving Associate scans ASN (Advance Shipping Notice) barcode from vendor packing slip; (d) system matches ASN to PO: quantities, SKUs, lot numbers verified; (e) any discrepancies (short ship, over ship, wrong SKU) flagged for resolution; (f) accepted goods posted to inventory and PO closed; (g) vendor invoice matched to PO and receipt per PA-15.1 three-way match process
Responsible (R): Receiving Associate / Vendor Account Manager
Accountable (A): Merchandise Planner
Duration: Per receipt: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1495_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1495_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1495_Task10" name="Monthly VMI performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly VMI performance review: Monthly: (a) Merchandise Planner generates VMI scorecard per vendor: (i) fill rate (target &gt; 97%); (ii) on-time delivery (target &gt; 95%); (iii) PO accuracy — correct quantity and SKU (target &gt; 99%); (iv) days of inventory on hand vs. target; (v) stock-out incidents; (b) vendors below target thresholds receive performance improvement notice; (c) consistently underperforming vendors (&lt; 90% fill rate for 3 consecutive months) removed from VMI program and revert to BuildRight-managed replenishment; (d) top-performing vendors considered for expanded VMI scope; (e) scorecard shared with vendor through portal
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1495_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1495_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1495_Task11" name="Quarterly VMI program evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly VMI program evaluation: Quarterly: (a) Category Manager reviews overall VMI program: (i) total VMI SKUs and vendors; (ii) aggregate in-stock rate vs. non-VMI; (iii) inventory turns for VMI items vs. non-VMI; (iv) carrying cost savings from vendor-managed replenishment; (v) new vendor candidates for VMI expansion; (b) program expansion decision: add/remove categories, add/remove vendors; (c) updated VMI vendor roster and SKU list communicated to affected teams
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1495_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1495_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1495_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1495_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1495_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-249 (ensure controlled execution — Vendor Portal &amp; Collaboration (PA-03.4).) | - operational: Merchandise Planner review and approval gate
Owner: Merchandise Planner</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
